  "notes": [
    "Traits are a first-class dataset (traits.json) referenced by Persona.traitId, not injected into learn-sets at level 0 (§8.2 note 5).",
    "`resmods` dropped (§14 Q3): three personas carry per-element damage multipliers that affect no calculation this app performs.",
    "Party personas keep upstream `statsm` as `maxStats` and have `growth: null`; their second affinity string (`sesists`) is dropped — its meaning is not documented upstream.",
    "Shadow `trait` dropped: §5 does not model it, and on sub-bosses upstream stores the human name rather than a persona trait.",
    "Skill `c[2]` is a list of in-world card locations (chests, Jazz Jin dates, trials), not a §5 cardSources origin; imported as `cardLocations`. The three §6.6 origins are derived from persona itemization and shadow negotiation.",
    "236 of the 464 persona itemization results are accessories or gear rather than skill cards; those keep the raw name on `normalItem`/`alarmItem` and leave the skill id null.",
    "roy-accessories.json imported (§14 Q4): all 125 accessory → skill mappings resolve to real skills.",
    "Classroom answers (§8.3) have no machine-readable upstream; they are transcribed from a user-supplied reference (classroom-data.mjs) and carry that URL as a per-record source. Answers cross-checked across three independent P5R guides."
  ],
